    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stonehill/jobs/5471700/professor-of-practice-in-environmental-science": {
      "title": "Professor of Practice in Environmental Science",
      "description": "Professor of Practice in Environmental Science Salary $71,000.00 - $75,000.00 Annually Location Easton, MA Job Type Faculty Benefit Eligible Job Number 00043 Department Environmental Studies Salaries Opening Date 09/03/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit N/A Description Benefits Founded by the Congregation of Holy Cross in 1948, Stonehill is a private Catholic college located just 22 miles from downtown Boston on a beautiful 384-acre campus in Easton, Massachusetts. With a student-to-faculty ratio of 13:1, the College engages its 2,500+ students in 80+ rigorous academic programs in the liberal arts, sciences, and pre-professional fields. Faithful to the Holy Cross tradition in education, Stonehill College is committed to developing the moral, spiritual, intellectual, physical, and social competencies of its students and seeks to build and sustain a campus community that embraces diversity and inclusion in its teaching, learning, living, and working. Stonehill values a diversity of persons, opinions, and cultural and religious perspectives. In fulfillment of its motto, Lux et Spes (“Light and Hope”), the College cultivates in its students the competence to think, act, and lead with courage towards creating a more just and compassionate world. Description The Environmental Science & Studies Department at Stonehill College invites applications for a full-time Professor of Practice faculty position with a focus in Environmental Health and Environmental Justice, beginning Fall 2027. We seek a colleague whose teaching engages the intersections of environmental science, public health, and social equity, someone who can help students understand not only the mechanisms of environmental harm, but who bears its burdens, and why. The department supports a B.A. in Environmental Studies, a B.S. in Environmental Science, a 3+2 Environmental Engineering Dual Degree with the University of Notre Dame, and an affiliated minor. Responsibilities · Teach undergraduate courses spanning environmental health, environmental justice, environmental writing, and related topics across the B.A. and B.S. curricula. · The successful candidate will teach four classes each semester. The courses will likely be a mix of general education classes and those designed for upper-level ENV majors. · Collaborate with ENV, Nursing, and Health Science faculty as well as the Stonehill Farm on environmental health issues. · Develop a dedicated focus in Environmental Health within the department. · Mentor and advise undergraduate students, including potential supervision of community-engaged and place-based research. · Contribute to departmental governance, curriculum development, and college-wide service. Areas of Expertise · Environmental justice and health equity · Social determinants of environmental health · Climate change and unequal health burdens · Toxic exposure, pollution, and environmental racism · Community and occupational health disparities · Environmental policy and regulatory frameworks as they intersect with public health Typical Qualifications · Ph.D. in Environmental Science, Environmental Health, Public Health, or a closely related field. · Commitment to undergraduate teaching and mentorship in a liberal arts setting. · Demonstrated commitment to inclusive teaching and to working with a diverse student body. · Experience or interest in interdisciplinary collaboration with nursing, public health, or health science programs. Supplemental Information Interested applicants are asked to submit a CV and cover letter online. The review of applications will begin on November 1, 2026. Stonehill College offers a comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees, based on position, which includes: Medical, prescription drug, vision, and dental coverage Paid vacation, holidays, and various leave programs Competitive retirement benefits, including defined contribution plans and voluntary tax-deferred savings options Employee and dependent educational benefits Life insurance coverage Employee discount programs Voluntray benefits For detailed information on benefits and eligibility, please visit here for more information. Employer Stonehill College (MA) Address 320 Washington Street Easton, Massachusetts, 02357 Phone 508-565-1105 Website www.stonehill.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stonehill/jobs/5504894/professor-of-practice-in-finance": {
      "title": "Professor of Practice in Finance",
      "description": "Professor of Practice in Finance Salary $103,280.00 - $108,552.00 Annually Location Easton, MA Job Type Faculty Benefit Eligible Job Number 00055 Department Finance Salaries Opening Date 10/05/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit N/A Description Benefits Founded by the Congregation of Holy Cross in 1948, Stonehill is a private Catholic college located just 22 miles from downtown Boston on a beautiful 384-acre campus in Easton, Massachusetts. With a student-to-faculty ratio of 13:1, the College engages its 2,500+ students in 80+ rigorous academic programs in the liberal arts, sciences, and pre-professional fields. Faithful to the Holy Cross tradition in education, Stonehill College is committed to developing the moral, spiritual, intellectual, physical, and social competencies of its students and seeks to build and sustain a campus community that embraces diversity and inclusion in its teaching, learning, living, and working. Stonehill values a diversity of persons, opinions, and cultural and religious perspectives. In fulfillment of its motto, Lux et Spes (“Light and Hope”), the College cultivates in its students the competence to think, act, and lead with courage towards creating a more just and compassionate world. Description The Department of Finance in the Leo J. Meehan School of Business at Stonehill College invites applicants for a Professor of Practice position in Finance beginning Fall 2027. The incoming faculty member would be part of a diverse and inclusive faculty with a wide range of disciplinary expertise. This position carries a non-tenure-track status. This is a full-time on-campus position, and a qualified candidate must teach on the physical Stonehill College campus. The Meehan School of Business is home to a state-of-the-art instructional facility built in August 2019. The business and innovation activities housed in the new building include a team-based learning classroom, one-button studio, and Capital Markets research and instruction room. The adaptive classrooms with the latest technology encourage interdisciplinary student, faculty, and industry interactions. The Bachelor of Science in Business Administration program in the Meehan School of Business is AACSB-accredited and offers majors in Accounting, Business Analytics, Finance, International Business, Management, Management Information Systems, Marketing, Sport Management, and Talent & Human Resources Management. The Meehan School of Business also offers minors in Business, Data Analytics, Economics, Entrepreneurship, and Healthcare Management. At the graduate level, Stonehill College offers a Master of Business Administration (MBA), as well as a Master of Professional Studies in Data Analytics and a Master of Science in Marketing. Responsibilities The selected candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate courses. The course load is 8 classes per academic year (i.e., 4 per semester) and may include: - Corporate Finance - Investments - Financial Literacy - Portfolio Management - Equity Research - Wealth Management - Financial Technology The faculty member will serve as advisor to Stonehill College's Financial Management Association (FMA) chapter and actively support student professional development through programming, mentoring, and engagement with finance professionals. Responsibilities will include maintaining and strengthening relationships with FMA chapter alumni to foster networking, mentoring, and career opportunities for students. Consistent with Stonehill College's commitment to student recruitment and engagement, the successful candidate will be expected to participate in undergraduate admission activities, including Open Houses and Admitted Student Welcome Days. The faculty member will also contribute to virtual and in-person engagement initiatives designed to connect prospective students and their families with the Finance program and the broader Stonehill community. Typical Qualifications We seek applicants with a strong interest in teaching and applied practice in finance. Candidates must, at a minimum, hold an MBA with a concentration in finance or an MS degree in finance. A Chartered Financial Analyst (CFA) designation is highly desirable. The applicant must show a strong interest in teaching and mentoring undergraduate students and enjoy working closely with student advisees to establish academic and professional goals. The successful candidate will be expected to contribute to Stonehill College's commitment to experiential education and will advise and mentor students through experiential learning opportunities, including oversight of the student-managed investment fund. Supplemental Information Interested applicants should submit online a cover letter, curriculum vitae, evidence of teaching effectiveness (such as summaries of student evaluations, if available), and two letters of reference. Please submit required documentation through the job site. Please email inquiries regarding this position to Dr. Elif Sisli Ciamarra at esisliciamarr@stonehill.edu. Applicants who will enrich the diversity of the campus community are strongly encouraged to apply. Stonehill College is an equal opportunity employer committed to diversity. Stonehill College offers a comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees, based on position, which includes: Medical, prescription drug, vision, and dental coverage Paid vacation, holidays, and various leave programs Competitive retirement benefits, including defined contribution plans and voluntary tax-deferred savings options Employee and dependent educational benefits Life insurance coverage Employee discount programs Voluntray benefits For detailed information on benefits and eligibility, please visit here for more information. Employer Stonehill College (MA) Address 320 Washington Street Easton, Massachusetts, 02357 Phone 508-565-1105 Website www.stonehill.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stonehill/jobs/5516231/professor-of-practice-in-healthcare-management": {
      "title": "Professor of Practice In Healthcare Management",
      "description": "Professor of Practice In Healthcare Management Salary $89,680.00 - $94,260.00 Annually Location Easton, MA Job Type Faculty Benefit Eligible Job Number 00058 Department Health Care Administration Salaries Opening Date 10/14/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit N/A Description Benefits Founded by the Congregation of Holy Cross in 1948, Stonehill is a private Catholic college located just 22 miles from downtown Boston on a beautiful 384-acre campus in Easton, Massachusetts. With a student-to-faculty ratio of 13:1, the College engages its 2,500+ students in 80+ rigorous academic programs in the liberal arts, sciences, and pre-professional fields. Faithful to the Holy Cross tradition in education, Stonehill College is committed to developing the moral, spiritual, intellectual, physical, and social competencies of its students and seeks to build and sustain a campus community that embraces diversity and inclusion in its teaching, learning, living, and working. Stonehill values a diversity of persons, opinions, and cultural and religious perspectives. In fulfillment of its motto, Lux et Spes (“Light and Hope”), the College cultivates in its students the competence to think, act, and lead with courage towards creating a more just and compassionate world. Description The Department of Healthcare Management in the Leo J. Meehan School of Business at Stonehill College invites applicants for a Professor of Practice position in Healthcare Management beginning Fall 2027. This person would join a department with faculty representing a wide range of disciplinary expertise and a commitment to fostering diversity and inclusion among faculty and students. This position carries a non-tenure-track status and is eligible for advancement and promotion. This is a full-time on-campus position, and a qualified candidate must teach on the physical Stonehill College campus. The Meehan School of Business is home to a state-of-the-art instructional facility completed in August 2019. The business and innovation activities housed in the new building include team-based learning classrooms, a one-button studio, and a capital markets research and instruction room. The adaptive classrooms with the latest technology encourage interdisciplinary student, faculty, and industry interactions. The Bachelor of Arts in Healthcare Management Program in the Meehan School of Business maintains full certification status with the Association of University Programs in Health Administration. The AACSB-accredited Meehan School of Business also offers minors in Business, Data Analytics, Economics, Entrepreneurship, and Healthcare Management. At the graduate level, Stonehill College offers a Master of Business Administration (MBA), as well as a Master of Science in Data Analytics and a Master of Science in Marketing. Responsibilities The selected candidate will deliver courses at the undergraduate level. The course load is 8 courses per academic year (4 per semester) and may include: · Quality Improvement and Methods in Healthcare · Computers in Healthcare Management · Healthcare Data Analysis · Healthcare Foundations (Intro to the U.S. health system) · Other courses offered by the Department Typical Qualifications We seek applicants with a strong interest in teaching and applied practice in the fields of Healthcare Management, specifically healthcare operations and technology. Candidates must hold at least a master’s degree (e.g., MHA, MBA, Master of Science). Preferred areas of expertise include professional responsibility and ethics, quality improvement (especially Lean thinking approaches), electronic medical records, AI implementation in healthcare, telehealth, and data analytics. Professional certification (e.g., higher-level Lean certification), undergraduate teaching experience, current professional practice, and ongoing engagement with the professional community are strongly preferred. A commitment to service to the Department, School, and College is also essential. The applicant must show a strong interest in teaching and mentoring undergraduate students and enjoy working closely with student advisees to establish academic and professional goals. Consistent with Stonehill College's commitment to student recruitment and engagement, the successful candidate will be expected to participate in undergraduate admission activities, including Open Houses and Admitted Student Welcome Days. The faculty member will also contribute to virtual and in-person engagement initiatives designed to connect prospective students and their families with the Healthcare Management Program and the broader Stonehill community. Supplemental Information Interested applicants should submit online a letter of application (cover letter), curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy statement, and evidence of teaching effectiveness (such as summaries of student evaluations), if available. References will be asked for at later stages. Please email inquiries regarding this position to Dr. Mitchell Glavin at mglavin@stonehill.edu. Stonehill College offers a comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees, based on position, which includes: Medical, prescription drug, vision, and dental coverage Paid vacation, holidays, and various leave programs Competitive retirement benefits, including defined contribution plans and voluntary tax-deferred savings options Employee and dependent educational benefits Life insurance coverage Employee discount programs Voluntray benefits For detailed information on benefits and eligibility, please visit here for more information. Employer Stonehill College (MA) Address 320 Washington Street Easton, Massachusetts, 02357 Phone 508-565-1105 Website www.stonehill.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stonehill/jobs/5500892/program-supervisor-for-graduate-teacher-education-program": {
      "title": "Program Supervisor for Graduate Teacher Education Program",
      "description": "Program Supervisor for Graduate Teacher Education Program Salary $1,000.00 - $3,000.00 Biweekly Location Easton, MA Job Type Admin Non-Benefit Eligible Job Number 00054 Department Graduate Teacher Ed Salaries Opening Date 09/30/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit N/A Description Benefits Founded by the Congregation of Holy Cross in 1948, Stonehill is a private Catholic college located just 22 miles from downtown Boston on a beautiful 384-acre campus in Easton, Massachusetts. With a student-to-faculty ratio of 13:1, the College engages its 2,500+ students in 80+ rigorous academic programs in the liberal arts, sciences, and pre-professional fields. Faithful to the Holy Cross tradition in education, Stonehill College is committed to developing the moral, spiritual, intellectual, physical, and social competencies of its students and seeks to build and sustain a campus community that embraces diversity and inclusion in its teaching, learning, living, and working. Stonehill values a diversity of persons, opinions, and cultural and religious perspectives. In fulfillment of its motto, Lux et Spes (“Light and Hope”), the College cultivates in its students the competence to think, act, and lead with courage towards creating a more just and compassionate world. Description The Division of Graduate and Professional Studies provides academic leadership and oversight of the College’s graduate and professional programs. GPS offers in-person, hybrid, and fully online master’s degrees, graduate certificates, and professional development in business, education, and experienced science programs. Our academic programs are designed to empower working professionals and recent graduates to expand their employment and career opportunities through rigorous, convenient, and flexible academic offerings. Responsibilities Stonehill College Division of Graduate and Professional Studies (GPS) at Stonehill College invites applicants for the position of Practicum Program Supervisor. The successful candidate for the position will support Stonehill graduate students who are in full-practicum placements as part of their progress towards licensure in Special Education and Humanities 5-8. The Program Supervisor serves as liaison between Stonehill College and the practicum placement site. The Program Supervisor is specifically responsible for the following: · Supporting the teacher candidate throughout the practicum semester (Jan-May), including providing oral and written feedback, conducting observations, and answer teacher candidate answering questions. · Conducting a minimum of 3 in-person observations and providing written feedback using DESE’s observation rubric; · Meeting with the teacher candidate and supervising practitioner at least 3 times during the spring to review strengths and areas for growth; · Reviewing and submitting all documentation required for licensure by the state Department of Elementary and Secondary Education; · Attending all relevant trainings and meetings with Stonehill’s Graduate Teacher Education Department; · Modeling best practices related to inclusive and culturally sustaining education. The Program Supervisor reports to the Coordinator of Clinical Practice and collaborates closely with the Graduate Teacher Education Department as well as supervising practitioners to ensure that Stonehill graduate teacher candidates receive the support and mentorship necessary for future success in their careers as PK-12 teachers. Typical Qualifications Minimum Qualifications (Knowledge, Skills, Abilities, Education, Experience, Certifications, Licensure) · Master’s degree in Education, Human Development, or a related field; · Minimum three (3) years of professional work experience in PK-12 education; · Exceptional interpersonal skills; · High level of written and oral communication; · Strong organizational and planning skills; · Ability to take initiative and work independently; · Ability to work collaboratively as a member of a team; · Ability to exercise discretion and confidentiality while interacting with a diverse student, faculty, and staff population; · Open to using and experimenting with technology in order to develop systems, increase efficiency and effectiveness. · Access to an automobile is required, as well as the ability to travel to practicum host sites – mostly located in eastern and southeastern Massachusetts – during the traditional school day; · Availability to mentor one or more teacher candidates; · Strong communication and organizational skills; · Commitment to mentoring the next generation of MA PK-12 teachers; · Strong interest in mentoring graduate students and enjoy working closely with teacher candidates to establish professional practice goals; · Contributing to implementation of departmental, divisional, and institutional goals for achieving non-discrimination and creating a respectful, inclusive environment that embraces diversity; · Maintaining confidentiality of student records. Preferred Qualifications · Active licensure as a Special Education or Humanities teacher; · Work experience in student mentorship; · Knowledge of Massachusetts teacher preparation regulatory expectations. Supplemental Information Stonehill College will provide formal onboarding for all practicum supervisors and ongoing support throughout the spring in addition to a $1000 stipend for each teacher candidate that you supervise. This position is not eligible for benefits. Employer Stonehill College (MA) Address 320 Washington Street Easton, Massachusetts, 02357 Phone 508-565-1105 Website www.stonehill.edu Apply"
    }
  },
